WEBVTT

00:26.710 --> 00:29.130
It was a long night...

00:32.970 --> 00:34.860
<i>N-Narukara-san?</i>

00:40.550 --> 00:44.140
She ended up coming back to my room.

00:44.630 --> 00:47.230
And she hasn't said a word since then.

00:47.800 --> 00:51.860
Was she really tired? She just fell asleep...

00:51.860 --> 00:54.150
What happened?

00:59.920 --> 01:02.790
Y-You'll catch a cold...

01:12.120 --> 01:13.920
I'm sorry.

01:15.250 --> 01:16.840
Father...

01:19.850 --> 01:23.450
Morning, Taketo! Are you still asleep?

01:23.450 --> 01:25.100
Fine, then...

01:25.740 --> 01:28.110
I'm in a hurry. I'll have to leave without you.

01:33.610 --> 01:35.110
Good morning.

01:35.110 --> 01:37.910
My heart throbs as I really do love you!

01:46.460 --> 01:51.500
These fifteen secrets in my head are written in letters, tucked away in my uniform.

01:51.500 --> 01:57.090
When you keep on making circles around me, in the middle of the launch of your image,

01:57.930 --> 02:02.640
you treat me kindly even with your mean look and puffed cheeks.

02:02.640 --> 02:08.310
For your first heart-throbbing, I'm sure you'll find it tremendous!

02:08.850 --> 02:11.770
Your voice will escape daringly!

02:11.770 --> 02:14.650
What you want to make your heart tingle, tell me!

02:14.650 --> 02:17.570
Quick! Let me! Where do you want what?! Seriously, you're terrible!

02:17.570 --> 02:19.570
These wild ideas have all detonated!

02:19.570 --> 02:22.410
I want to try and swallow more

02:22.410 --> 02:25.580
I want you to pet me more

02:25.580 --> 02:28.410
What kind of flavor is your heart?

02:28.410 --> 02:31.290
Someday, I'll be sure to grasp a hold of what's real

02:31.290 --> 02:33.590
I want to embrace you more

02:33.590 --> 02:36.800
Will you secretly let me see you?

02:36.840 --> 02:39.680
I can't get enough of this dream I'm having!

02:39.680 --> 02:45.060
Be it my heart or also my body, I'll hand them over since it's you.

02:42.890 --> 02:47.640
My heart throbs as I really do love you! (Look here!)

02:48.520 --> 02:53.810
My heart throbs as I really do love you!

03:05.700 --> 03:09.710
"Our Summertime Blue"

03:12.070 --> 03:14.060
It's really great,

03:14.060 --> 03:16.590
this song Iikyoku Kanade-san wrote.

03:17.660 --> 03:19.300
Something's missing.

03:19.380 --> 03:21.340
Iikyoku

03:19.380 --> 03:21.340
Kanade

03:20.420 --> 03:21.340
Songwriter

03:20.630 --> 03:21.340
Genius

03:21.340 --> 03:25.140
Y-You're right. The lyrics aren't done yet.

03:25.140 --> 03:30.580
But are you sure about this?
Having Akutagawa-kun write the lyrics?

03:30.580 --> 03:34.360
He's the only one with any kind of
writing talent in our class.

03:34.360 --> 03:36.770
Even if he is a genius porno author...

03:36.770 --> 03:42.920
With Narukara-san's accompaniment,
we're sure to win the chorus competition.

03:42.920 --> 03:45.780
But where are they?

03:56.130 --> 04:01.560
<i>You hugged me, out of the blue...
What happened, Narukara-san?</i>

04:01.560 --> 04:04.420
<i>I have to ask. </i>

04:04.420 --> 04:07.810
<i>I don't understand...</i>

04:10.300 --> 04:15.750
Lunch break, huh?
I've never skipped school in my life.

04:15.750 --> 04:17.250
Me, neither.

04:18.300 --> 04:22.760
I've never stayed home from school...

04:23.390 --> 04:25.200
without telling anyone.

04:26.880 --> 04:30.700
<i>I shouldn't be smiling now! Stupid!</i>

04:39.210 --> 04:43.580
Our next item is Utae-chan's favorite bear!

04:43.580 --> 04:47.720
She's used this bear for a lot,
and any fan would want it.

04:47.720 --> 04:49.720
Let's start at 5,000 yen!

04:49.720 --> 04:51.970
This goes over here, and that goes over there...

04:53.240 --> 04:57.980
Helping to run things might be harder than
actually participating in the orientation!

04:59.660 --> 05:01.430
120,000 yen!

05:01.430 --> 05:03.790
120,000 yen! Is that the high bid?

05:03.790 --> 05:04.990
125,000 yen!

05:13.450 --> 05:15.120
Things are really heating up...

05:15.120 --> 05:16.960
133,000!

05:21.610 --> 05:23.460
Utae-chan?

05:23.980 --> 05:28.960
Class 2 is using Utae-chan for the
money-making round, huh?

05:28.960 --> 05:31.350
We're doing fine, too.

05:32.480 --> 05:37.560
We have the genius programmer and
the genius mathematician teaming up!

05:38.780 --> 05:40.980
A-About that...

05:43.110 --> 05:45.960
What happened to those two?

05:51.990 --> 05:56.720
Ritsu's complicated
economic-forecasting formula,

05:56.720 --> 06:02.000
and Ran's program, which instantly
responds to worldwide conditions.

06:02.470 --> 06:06.010
Working together, they became
overnight millionaires!

06:06.010 --> 06:07.850
We did it!

06:07.850 --> 06:10.510
Did you guys convert that to cash?

06:11.010 --> 06:15.030
The round two rules stated to raise cash.

06:15.030 --> 06:16.990
Computer data...

06:16.990 --> 06:18.100
...doesn't count.

06:25.110 --> 06:27.370
In the second round,

06:27.370 --> 06:29.580
class 1-2 wins, with 200 points.

06:29.580 --> 06:32.440
Class 1-1 gets 100 points.

06:32.440 --> 06:34.200
Coming in third,

06:34.200 --> 06:36.880
1-3 receives nothing!

06:36.880 --> 06:39.510
My theory was perfect.

06:39.510 --> 06:41.700
But... But...

06:42.910 --> 06:46.590
Our only hope now is to stage a
comeback in the chorus battle!

06:46.590 --> 06:50.240
I don't like having that
ero-idiot writing the lyrics...

06:50.860 --> 06:54.480
But with Fukune-chan's clarinet, we'll be fine!

06:54.480 --> 06:56.600
Right, Fukune-chan?

07:03.790 --> 07:07.210
Aw, don't worry about it...

07:07.210 --> 07:08.110
No.

07:08.560 --> 07:13.740
You made coffee for me, so at least let me make you lunch.

07:14.340 --> 07:15.760
Wait just a little longer.

07:16.980 --> 07:20.680
<i>This is great... It's like we're newlyweds.</i>

07:20.680 --> 07:24.500
<i>No, like a couple that's just started dating!</i>

07:24.510 --> 07:25.770
No, no!

07:25.770 --> 07:28.000
No, I need to ask what happened...

07:28.000 --> 07:29.920
What's this smell?

07:31.430 --> 07:33.800
It's burning!

07:41.320 --> 07:42.690
Are you sad?

07:42.690 --> 07:46.480
No... It's so good, I'm crying.

07:46.480 --> 07:48.040
That's great!

07:48.040 --> 07:50.110
I've never made these before.

07:50.110 --> 07:52.420
I'll make them again, okay?

07:52.420 --> 07:55.200
S-Some other time, sure...

07:59.160 --> 08:03.100
Hey, isn't it almost time for practice?

08:03.100 --> 08:04.890
You can do it here if you want.

08:04.890 --> 08:07.170
No, that's all right.

08:07.810 --> 08:09.300
Narukara-san?

08:11.020 --> 08:14.260
Oh, right. I mentioned this a little yesterday...

08:14.260 --> 08:17.440
But for the orientation tournament
chorus battle,

08:17.440 --> 08:19.930
would you play your clarinet for us?

08:23.070 --> 08:26.990
W-We're sure to win if you'll help us!

08:26.990 --> 08:31.690
But first, I have to write the lyrics...

08:33.330 --> 08:34.450
Lyrics?

08:34.450 --> 08:36.720
You're writing them?

08:36.720 --> 08:38.190
Y-Yeah.

08:38.190 --> 08:40.200
Everyone asked me to.

08:40.200 --> 08:43.330
What kind? What kind of lyrics are you writing?

08:44.300 --> 08:46.050
What kind...

08:46.050 --> 08:47.710
Well...

08:47.710 --> 08:50.380
But I can only write porn.

08:53.220 --> 08:55.510
<i>Fukune-san would understand!</i>

08:55.510 --> 08:58.510
U-U-Uh...

09:00.500 --> 09:05.600
Uh, about eternal love...
How you can't abandon your dreams!

09:05.600 --> 09:09.320
Or the treasure of friendship!
Maybe something like that...

09:11.240 --> 09:12.610
That's amazing.

09:13.680 --> 09:16.950
You really <i>are</i> a genius...

09:17.830 --> 09:21.550
You're totally different than me.

09:21.550 --> 09:23.250
Narukara-san?

09:29.460 --> 09:31.680
That's not true.

09:31.680 --> 09:34.210
You have something you care about.

09:34.210 --> 09:35.290
See?

09:39.860 --> 09:41.070
Akutagawa-kun...

09:41.980 --> 09:42.720
I...

09:42.720 --> 09:45.360
You're far more amazing than I am.

09:45.360 --> 09:47.640
You're a genius!

09:55.120 --> 09:57.300
So don't look like that...

09:57.300 --> 10:00.540
Everyone's counting on your clarinet.

10:00.540 --> 10:01.510
No...

10:03.170 --> 10:04.690
Narukara-san?

10:05.800 --> 10:07.180
I'm not a genius.

10:08.010 --> 10:09.420
I can't do it...

10:09.420 --> 10:12.420
The music didn't choose me.

10:13.210 --> 10:14.710
I'm not a genius...

10:14.710 --> 10:16.590
I'm not a genius at all!

10:16.590 --> 10:19.070
Not even with the clarinet...

10:19.070 --> 10:22.510
I've never enjoyed it or thought it was fun!

10:25.520 --> 10:27.890
I hate everything about it!

10:42.680 --> 10:44.070
Fukune-san?

10:57.340 --> 11:00.050
Narukara Fukune Withdraws

10:57.340 --> 11:00.050
from Inspiration Academy?

11:00.480 --> 11:02.550
What is this?

11:02.550 --> 11:07.020
Fukune Narukara-san,
clarinet genius from 1-3,

11:07.020 --> 11:10.080
has asked to withdraw from
Inspiration Academy.

11:10.080 --> 11:15.070
This decision appears to be
motivated by her father,

11:15.070 --> 11:18.350
Narukara Fukuzoushi, one of
the world's greatest clarinet players.

11:18.350 --> 11:20.650
Narukara-san's going to a different school.

11:20.650 --> 11:23.070
That's way bigger than this chorus thing...

11:23.800 --> 11:25.150
Taketo?

11:25.990 --> 11:28.500
NEWSPAPER

11:25.990 --> 11:28.500
CIRCLE

11:25.990 --> 11:28.500
Is that article true?

11:28.500 --> 11:31.500
It's just a rumor, but yes.

11:31.500 --> 11:37.420
But as a genius, it may be better
that she studies across the world.

11:37.420 --> 11:39.670
Better for her?

11:39.670 --> 11:42.260
Don't say mean things like that!

11:43.590 --> 11:45.010
Please...

11:45.010 --> 11:47.300
Mean, huh?

11:47.300 --> 11:50.020
Then, did you know about this?

11:50.020 --> 11:55.150
Yesterday, Narukara-san's solo concert
was a huge disaster.

11:59.650 --> 12:01.290
Halfway through the performance,

12:01.290 --> 12:04.120
she stopped being able
to play, for some reason.

12:04.120 --> 12:07.160
The staff didn't know what else to do,
except lower the curtain.

12:12.430 --> 12:16.040
And then, she didn't return
to her dorm afterward.

12:16.040 --> 12:18.460
She went and hid somewhere.

12:19.010 --> 12:21.020
She probably felt so terrible,

12:21.020 --> 12:24.470
she just wanted someone
to make her feel better...

12:28.470 --> 12:29.970
Fukune-chan!

12:29.970 --> 12:33.200
It's not true, is it?
You're not leaving, right?

12:33.200 --> 12:34.730
Right? Right?!

12:34.730 --> 12:36.450
Fukune-chan!

12:37.730 --> 12:40.100
No response, huh?

12:40.910 --> 12:42.490
Then I'll force my way in!

12:44.530 --> 12:46.660
Come on, Ran... Calm down!

12:46.660 --> 12:48.170
But why did this happen, all of a sudden?

12:48.170 --> 12:52.370
Why? No one's seen her
since the concert ended.

12:52.370 --> 12:56.250
I didn't see Akutagawa-kun yesterday, either.

12:56.250 --> 12:57.740
Taketo?

13:03.120 --> 13:07.610
If I'd known what was going on
with Narukara-san...

13:08.900 --> 13:11.800
If you'd known what was going on?

13:15.880 --> 13:18.440
What happened to her?

13:20.080 --> 13:22.570
She was in your room?!

13:24.620 --> 13:29.610
When she was feeling her worst,
she chose you, not me.

13:29.610 --> 13:30.830
Fukune-chan...

13:31.590 --> 13:32.690
Ran...

13:44.120 --> 13:45.260
However,

13:46.050 --> 13:48.600
I can't believe she'd leave the school.

13:48.600 --> 13:50.400
That she'd just disappear.

13:50.930 --> 13:52.250
I can't believe it!

13:53.310 --> 13:56.350
Why? Why did this happen?

13:56.350 --> 13:57.690
What should we do?

13:57.690 --> 14:00.600
I don't know what's happening anymore!

14:00.600 --> 14:02.520
I'm going to write those lyrics.

14:02.520 --> 14:05.820
What are you talking about?
This isn't the time to worry about that.

14:06.530 --> 14:07.570
That's why.

14:08.970 --> 14:11.510
There's no way that Narukara-san hates music.

14:11.510 --> 14:13.970
Or hates her clarinet.

14:13.970 --> 14:16.760
She might be closing off her heart right now.

14:17.600 --> 14:20.170
But music is the only way to open it.

14:20.170 --> 14:22.800
We'll have to bet everything on our chorus!

14:22.800 --> 14:26.610
I'll show her who I really am...
I'll write porno lyrics!

14:29.840 --> 14:31.880
You may be right.

14:31.880 --> 14:35.650
I hate to admit it, but with your porno talents,

14:35.650 --> 14:38.100
you might write something incredible.

14:38.100 --> 14:40.400
I'm going to tell Narukara-san...

14:40.400 --> 14:44.730
With my lyrics, I'll tell her how I...
I mean, how we feel!

14:44.730 --> 14:46.660
Taketo!

14:46.660 --> 14:50.240
What are you two doing in there without me?

14:50.250 --> 14:52.740
We're getting started. All of us.

14:54.100 --> 14:55.320
Before that...

14:58.050 --> 14:59.380
Hang on to this.

15:00.030 --> 15:01.330
O-Okay...

15:07.170 --> 15:09.130
That's the price for holding her clarinet.

15:15.150 --> 15:20.230
But without lyrics or accompaniment,
isn't victory impossible?

15:21.230 --> 15:23.460
A genius doesn't acknowledge the impossible!

15:23.460 --> 15:26.230
Losing doesn't bother you?

15:27.270 --> 15:29.390
I guess we have no choice.

15:29.390 --> 15:32.240
At this rate, we can't call ourselves geniuses.

15:33.800 --> 15:35.240
Yeah.

15:36.830 --> 15:38.330
I'm going to write them!

15:38.330 --> 15:41.460
With the passion I put into
my pornographic novels,

15:41.460 --> 15:45.340
I'll write lyrics that stand up
proud, strong, and erect!

15:58.010 --> 15:59.560
I can't write...

15:59.560 --> 16:02.510
You're a genius, right?
How can writing lyrics scare you?

16:02.510 --> 16:05.560
Or can you not be a lyricist?
No, that's impossible!

16:05.560 --> 16:08.160
But if it were a pornographic novel...

16:10.620 --> 16:12.110
Awaken...

16:12.810 --> 16:15.330
To new heights, to new pleasures...

16:15.330 --> 16:17.080
To overflowing passion!

16:18.170 --> 16:19.900
Please tell me...

16:19.900 --> 16:24.330
I want you to use your talents
to show me what love truly is.

16:25.510 --> 16:28.870
I want you to fill me up with your emotion.

16:28.870 --> 16:30.490
Fill me up...

16:30.490 --> 16:33.840
I can feel it! It's overflowing!

16:49.600 --> 16:51.230
I can write them...

16:53.390 --> 16:54.740
Narukara-san.

16:54.740 --> 16:58.740
Just wait, Narukara-san.
I'm writing this for you.

17:01.300 --> 17:03.250
<i>What kind of lyrics are you writing?</i>

17:10.150 --> 17:12.700
<i>You really are a genius, Akutagawa-kun.</i>

17:15.220 --> 17:18.090
<i>You're totally different than Fukune.</i>

17:18.090 --> 17:21.420
<i>What are you writing?</i>

17:32.110 --> 17:35.610
I heard Akutagawa-kun writes porno novels!

17:35.610 --> 17:38.740
Oh, man. How creepy...
We'd better stay away from him.

17:38.740 --> 17:42.920
It's not like that! Pornography is an art, and...

17:42.920 --> 17:45.390
And I'm telling stories about love!

17:46.970 --> 17:48.120
I hate you.

17:57.050 --> 17:58.750
What am I doing?

18:00.050 --> 18:02.560
Inspiration Academy

18:00.050 --> 18:02.560
Newspaper Circle

18:05.630 --> 18:06.960
If it were me,

18:07.660 --> 18:09.600
I could be with you forever...

18:10.450 --> 18:12.070
Taketo-kun.

18:13.190 --> 18:14.070
Akutagawa Taketo-kun

18:16.800 --> 18:21.580
<i>Yeah... Somehow, your saying that
made me feel a lot better!</i>

18:26.080 --> 18:30.580
Inspiration Academy

18:26.080 --> 18:30.580
Newspaper Circle

18:26.450 --> 18:30.170
I'm becoming a horrible person.

18:31.520 --> 18:35.130
Go! Go! Utae!

18:35.840 --> 18:39.130
You can do it! You can do it, Utae!

18:39.130 --> 18:42.350
Fight! Fight! Utae!

18:46.430 --> 18:48.940
Ow...

18:48.940 --> 18:51.350
What are you doing, Katsuyo-san?

18:51.350 --> 18:53.490
What else?

18:53.490 --> 18:55.190
I'm cheering you on.

18:55.200 --> 18:56.690
Me?

18:58.980 --> 19:03.180
You looked like you were lonely, worrying a lot.

19:03.180 --> 19:05.160
So I came to cheer for you!

19:05.650 --> 19:09.080
Whatever happens, you should be
honest about your feelings.

19:09.080 --> 19:10.670
That's for the best!

19:10.670 --> 19:14.100
Go! Go! Utae!

19:14.100 --> 19:17.460
Fight! You can do it! Let's go!

19:17.460 --> 19:20.870
Cheer up, Utae-chan!

19:20.870 --> 19:23.680
Knock those tears out of the park!

19:31.280 --> 19:36.140
As I thought... School wasn't
something you needed.

19:37.140 --> 19:38.440
Father...

19:38.960 --> 19:43.330
You must be a genius at all times,
in all conditions.

19:43.330 --> 19:46.060
That is what your clarinet demands.

19:46.060 --> 19:48.950
That is why you exist.

19:56.000 --> 20:00.420
I love your music!

20:14.430 --> 20:16.980
"Love will never lose."

20:16.980 --> 20:20.380
"Do your best, and hope will find you."

20:20.380 --> 20:21.990
"Don't give up."

20:21.990 --> 20:24.810
"Your dream will come true."

20:26.620 --> 20:28.890
"I am always by your side."

20:32.500 --> 20:35.820
I could write all kinds of lyrics like those.

20:36.530 --> 20:37.500
That would...

20:37.500 --> 20:39.000
<i>I hate you.</i>

20:39.000 --> 20:42.670
It would keep her from hating me any more than she does now.

20:47.170 --> 20:48.970
I like that face.

20:48.970 --> 20:51.350
That's what I'm looking for in a photo.

20:51.350 --> 20:53.350
Raika.

20:53.350 --> 20:55.850
The ultimate ugliness...

20:58.860 --> 21:02.470
A man who abandons himself,
to run from everything.

21:02.470 --> 21:05.070
Well? Ugly, right?

21:08.080 --> 21:09.610
I...

21:09.610 --> 21:12.000
I don't have a choice!

21:12.000 --> 21:15.280
Do you know what the
ugliest thing in the world is?

21:15.280 --> 21:17.380
A liar.

21:20.530 --> 21:23.620
One who talks about opening a person's heart,

21:23.620 --> 21:26.120
but seals off their own.

21:26.120 --> 21:28.310
One who claims to want to save someone,

21:28.310 --> 21:30.970
but only talks about what's convenient.

21:30.970 --> 21:33.290
And in the end,

21:33.290 --> 21:36.520
excuses are all they have.

21:37.610 --> 21:40.520
I like that face. It's wonderful.

21:40.520 --> 21:43.530
An ugliness worthy of the title, "Liar."

21:44.200 --> 21:45.280
No.

21:46.360 --> 21:48.320
This isn't me.

21:48.320 --> 21:50.280
The real me...

21:55.760 --> 21:58.330
I'm not like that!

22:05.850 --> 22:10.900
I guess I failed as a cameraman,
becoming so involved with a subject.

22:10.900 --> 22:12.850
I'm horrible.

22:13.470 --> 22:17.290
So, I really am the ugliest of them all...

22:33.820 --> 22:36.730
Hey there, that FLASHY POWER needs more energy!

22:36.730 --> 22:39.770
Shout HURRAY, and raise the words of PEACE to the sky!

22:51.300 --> 22:54.220
Come, be HAPPY first thing in the morning; love KNOWS the outcome of the underwear battle!

22:54.220 --> 22:57.020
Hold on! Keep this a secret, it feels awfully squishy down below; it feels amazing.

22:57.020 --> 22:58.460
Since you're taking a peek, darling,

22:58.460 --> 22:59.870
shall I give you myself, you virgin!

22:59.870 --> 23:02.380
Oh my, you WARNING me about your arousal? I'm OKAY with that!

23:02.380 --> 23:07.950
Let's jump into the heaven that is a sparkling room!

23:07.950 --> 23:10.610
SAY EVERYBODY, we can reply to our pleasant feelings.

23:10.610 --> 23:13.070
It's time to run and PLAY BALL!

23:13.070 --> 23:15.990
Let's go! Long live PEACE! Don't give up PEACE!

23:15.990 --> 23:18.800
Today we'll surely have 'ecchi' moments,

23:18.800 --> 23:24.450
Raise your hands and JUMP! God of HIGH-TENSION, beware!

23:24.450 --> 23:27.460
Once more! Long live PEACE! Everything is all right, PEACE!

23:27.460 --> 23:30.210
